From c6dbeee416ec849cd7aa10fe68e90dcc35725a9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:10:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make Windows test teardown tolerant of SQLite file-lock
 timing

tempfile.TemporaryDirectory().cleanup() was racing a just-closed sqlite3
connection's file handle on Windows, failing with PermissionError during
tearDown -- after the actual test assertions had already passed. Not a
functional bug; ignore_cleanup_errors=True makes cleanup tolerate it
instead of raising.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E1cXxHLvxWsVApjc9w7bwH
